  "kind": "quirk",
  "title": "NOT rejects numeric strings such as \"1\" and empty strings with #VALUE!, accepting only numbers, logicals, and \"TRUE\"/\"FALSE\"",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20527.20088, NOT(logical) coerces its single scalar argument as a logical rather than a number: \"TRUE\" gives FALSE and \"false\" gives TRUE, whereas \"1\", \"\", and \"x\" all return #VALUE!. A blank cell evaluates to FALSE, so NOT(blank) returns TRUE.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in Excel 16.0.20527.20088 across rows 86-102 and 114-115 of dc_fwpz.",
